# REQUIRES: python-api
# Device-resident buffers of a persistent simulation on the CPU
# (D[resident-buffers]), scenario updates of Inputs/python_resident.py.
# Updates of tunables, evaluations, and reads of the state between parts:
# any partition of the steps after them gives the same state to the bit;
# an evaluation before the first run leaves the run that follows unchanged.
# RUN: %mdir_python %S/Inputs/python_resident.py %S/Inputs/dipeptide CPU updates | FileCheck %s
# CHECK: Double VelocityVerlet: after an update and an evaluation, parts of 12, 5+7, and 1+1+10 steps give the same state to the bit; an evaluation before the first run changes nothing
# CHECK: Double Leapfrog: after an update and an evaluation, parts of 12, 5+7, and 1+1+10 steps give the same state to the bit; an evaluation before the first run changes nothing
# CHECK: Mixed VelocityVerlet: after an update and an evaluation, parts of 12, 5+7, and 1+1+10 steps give the same state to the bit; an evaluation before the first run changes nothing
# CHECK: Mixed Leapfrog: after an update and an evaluation, parts of 12, 5+7, and 1+1+10 steps give the same state to the bit; an evaluation before the first run changes nothing
# CHECK: resident updates passed
